    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bennetts Auctioneers are delighted to bring No. 21 Margaret Place to the market. Ideally positioned on this quiet and highly sought-after residential road in Sandymount, this attractive three-bedroom semi-detached family home offers well-proportioned accommodation. The accommodation extends to approximately 84 sq. m. and briefly comprises an entrance hall, sitting room, living room, kitchen/dining room, bedroom and W.C. at ground-floor level. Two bedrooms and a shower room on the first floor complete the property. Features of the property include gas fired central heating, double glazed windows and rear pedestrian access.\r\n\r\nExternally, to the front a small, railed garden laid out in lawn, with convenient side access leading through to the rear. To the rear, a good sized private garden with convenient rear pedestrian access to adjacent laneway.\r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\nMargaret Place is ideally positioned just off Bath Avenue in this highly sought-after and convenient location. The property is within easy walking distance of an excellent selection of amenities, including shops, restaurants, cafés, schools and sporting facilities. The Aviva Stadium and RDS are located nearby, while both Sandymount and Ballsbridge Villages are within comfortable walking distance and offer an extensive range of shops, restaurants, bars and other amenities. There is an array of schools in the locality including Star of the Sea BNS, Scoil Mhuire GNS, St Christopher's BNS and St. Michaels, to name a few. Transport links are excellent, with Grand Canal Dock DART Station located within a 5 minute walk away, along with numerous bus routes serving the city centre and surrounding areas. The East Link Bridge provides easy access to Dublin Port and beyond, while Dublin city centre and the IFSC are just a short distance away."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall:  2.86m x 1.76m  tiled flooring, dado rail\r\n\r\nSitting room:  2.86m x 3.00m  carpet flooring, original fireplace, window to front  \r\n\r\nLiving  room:  3.38m x 4.86m  wood flooring, feature fireplace, window to side, door to under stairs storage, window to \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining room:  2.45m x 4.86m  wood flooring, range of floor an eye level units, fully plumbed for washer dryer, stainless steel sink, dual sky lights, large window to rear garden  \r\n\r\nBedroom 3:  3.90m x 2.35m  carpet flooring, large window to front garden\r\n\r\nW.C.:   0.88m x 1.61m   tiled throughout, W.C., W.H.B. \r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nBedroom 1:  3.34m x 4.86m  carpet flooring, built in wardrobe, hot press, window to front  \r\n\r\nBedroom 2:  2.90m x 3.32m  carpet flooring, window to rear\r\n\r\nShower room:  1.80m x 1.45m  tiled throughout, walk in shower unit, W.H.B., W.C., window to rear  \r\n\r\nTotal floor area: c.   84 sq. m\r\n\r\nTo the front, there is a small, railed garden laid out in lawn, with convenient side access leading to the rear. To the rear, a good-sized private garden which has the added also benefit of pedestrian access to the adjacent laneway, providing excellent convenience and additional accessibility. \r\n\r\nBER: F\r\n\r\nBER No:  109023978\r\n\r\nPerformance indicator:  345.54 kWh/m²/yr\r\n\r\nAsking price: €685,000\r\n\r\nNegotiator: Keith McCabe"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming three-bedroom semi-detached family home\r\n\r\nQuiet and highly sought-after Dublin 4 location\r\n\r\nGas fired central heating & double glazed windows throughout\r\n\r\nMinutes from Aviva Stadium, RDS, Silicon Docks and IFSC\r\n\r\nExcellent private rear garden with pedestrian rear access\r\n\r\nTotal floor area of approximately 84 sq. m.\r\n\r\nClose to a range of shops, restaurants and transport links"
